# Reference only — the Coordinator self-provisions these (PROMPT.md, SELF-PROVISIONED WAKE-UP).
# Markers are load-bearing: the coordinator finds/heals its entries by them. Never remove.
# Both entries run EVERY DAY — the human works every day; never restrict to weekdays.
# The cycle entry is adaptive: the coordinator keeps it only while the pipeline
# (Spec..CI Fixup) has tasks, and drops it when the pipeline is empty.
CRON_TZ=America/Toronto
0 8 * * * $HOME/.local/bin/kandev-coordinator-wake.sh STANDUP # kandev-coordinator-standup
*/45 8-22 * * * $HOME/.local/bin/kandev-coordinator-wake.sh CYCLE # kandev-coordinator-cycle

# Environments without a crontab binary (e.g. kandev worktree executor): the
# coordinator uses the agent-harness scheduler (CronList/CronCreate) with the
# same markers embedded in the job prompts. Harness jobs are session-scoped and
# auto-expire (~7 days), so they are re-verified and recreated on every wake-up.
# UTC equivalents used there (EDT): standup 57 11 * * *, cycle hourly 12-23,0-2.
